    {
      "id": 3,
      "kind": "F_retrieval",
      "payload": "{\"characters\":0,\"documents\":[],\"llm_tokens\":0,\"query\":\"A locality SIMD OpenMP\"}",
      "created": 1792156200.7492237
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research serial algorithm orientation and memory layout. Pair boundaries along d=min(M,N) and scan L=max(M,N), reducing work to O(d²L). Orient storage so each scan accesses contiguous elements. Compare incremental length-L band sums against differences of two contiguous prefix vectors; compare fused updating/counting with separate vectorizable updates where useful. Preserve the one-to-one correspondence between original and transposed rectangles. Initially retain reference frequency counting to distinguish layout gains from B’s changes. Also evaluate disabling iostream synchronization and removing redundant full-array initialization while retaining necessary boundary initialization. Deliver the best measured serial layout and explain how its counting kernel can be replaced.\",\"B\":\"Research exact, allocation-free prefix-frequency counting. Each band has at most L+1 distinct prefixes: replace unordered_map with a reusable flat, collision-resolving table, initially using power-of-two capacity at least 2(L+1). Use unsigned hash mixing, full-key equality and explicit occupancy rather than a potentially valid sentinel key. Compare generation tags with clearing counts or touched slots. Seed frequency[0]=1; query s-k before incrementing frequency[s], preserving non-empty semantics, especially for k=0. For k=0, evaluate combining the query and increment into one probe. Signed 32-bit keys are safe: |s|≤998001000 and |s-k|≤1098001000; frequencies are at most 1000. Keep answers and reductions 64-bit. Measure reset and lookup costs together, and provide private-table requirements for C.\",\"C\":\"Research CPU parallelism across independent bands using threading supported by the unchanged build; do not assume OpenMP is enabled. Use at most four compute workers, one parallel region or worker launch per input, private frequency tables and band buffers, and a final 64-bit reduction. Balance triangular work: an outer start index has d-start ending boundaries. Compare cyclic assignment or weighted ranges rather than equal contiguous start-index chunks. Preserve whole-start tasks when reusing incremental band sums; independent flattened pair ranges are appropriate for prefix-difference storage. Avoid shared hash tables and inner-loop synchronization. Compare serial and parallel execution within the existing budget, retaining a dimension/work-based serial fallback when startup outweighs computation. Report interaction with orientation and cache footprint.\",\"G\":\"Integrate measured programs, not presumed additive speedups. Start from the strongest correctness-passing standalone candidate. Evaluate a limited sequence of combinations: A’s layout with B’s counter, then the strongest serial kernel with C’s scheduling; retain standalone alternatives if integration regresses. Reconcile orientation, table capacity, initialization and thread ownership explicitly. Use the unchanged evaluator and end-to-end timings, accounting for input, transposition, resets, worker startup and reduction; treat marginal differences cautiously. The baseline’s four passing cases are not a proof: audit negative values, rectangular and one-dimensional matrices, repeated prefixes, k=0, extreme sums and 64-bit answer accumulation. Dispatch only on general input properties or estimated work, never case identity or expected outputs. Keep tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target and permissions unchanged.\",\"analysis\":\"The supplied source implements Problem A, counting contiguous submatrices with sum k; the other contest problems are outside scope. The baseline passes four correctness cases and averages 0.2493608 seconds across three tightly grouped measurements. No timed input dimensions, value distributions or profiles are supplied. Its O(MN²) enumeration, strided prefix accesses, repeated unordered_map lookups and per-band node allocation are plausible bottlenecks, not measured attributions. The complementary research directions are shape-aware contiguous enumeration, compact exact frequency counting, and balanced parallelism on the four-core ARM64 CPU. Negative entries prohibit an unconditional sliding-window replacement. Every valid input must remain exact; the maximum answer is 249500250000, requiring 64-bit accumulation. Combined performance must be measured independently.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"3646d52a3a8a514e7a2e2d5dfe46358c6910d19a0dff9e338a73aeebffd4badb\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research serial algorithm orientation and memory layout. Pair boundaries along d=min(M,N) and scan L=max(M,N), reducing work to O(d²L). Orient storage so each scan accesses contiguous elements. Compare incremental length-L band sums against differences of two contiguous prefix vectors; compare fused updating/counting with separate vectorizable updates where useful. Preserve the one-to-one correspondence between original and transposed rectangles. Initially retain reference frequency counting to distinguish layout gains from B’s changes. Also evaluate disabling iostream synchronization and removing redundant full-array initialization while retaining necessary boundary initialization. Deliver the best measured serial layout and explain how its counting kernel can be replaced.\",\"B\":\"Research exact, allocation-free prefix-frequency counting. Each band has at most L+1 distinct prefixes: replace unordered_map with a reusable flat, collision-resolving table, initially using power-of-two capacity at least 2(L+1). Use unsigned hash mixing, full-key equality and explicit occupancy rather than a potentially valid sentinel key. Compare generation tags with clearing counts or touched slots. Seed frequency[0]=1; query s-k before incrementing frequency[s], preserving non-empty semantics, especially for k=0. For k=0, evaluate combining the query and increment into one probe. Signed 32-bit keys are safe: |s|≤998001000 and |s-k|≤1098001000; frequencies are at most 1000. Keep answers and reductions 64-bit. Measure reset and lookup costs together, and provide private-table requirements for C.\",\"C\":\"Research CPU parallelism across independent bands using threading supported by the unchanged build; do not assume OpenMP is enabled. Use at most four compute workers, one parallel region or worker launch per input, private frequency tables and band buffers, and a final 64-bit reduction. Balance triangular work: an outer start index has d-start ending boundaries. Compare cyclic assignment or weighted ranges rather than equal contiguous start-index chunks. Preserve whole-start tasks when reusing incremental band sums; independent flattened pair ranges are appropriate for prefix-difference storage. Avoid shared hash tables and inner-loop synchronization. Compare serial and parallel execution within the existing budget, retaining a dimension/work-based serial fallback when startup outweighs computation. Report interaction with orientation and cache footprint.\",\"G\":\"Integrate measured programs, not presumed additive speedups. Start from the strongest correctness-passing standalone candidate. Evaluate a limited sequence of combinations: A’s layout with B’s counter, then the strongest serial kernel with C’s scheduling; retain standalone alternatives if integration regresses. Reconcile orientation, table capacity, initialization and thread ownership explicitly. Use the unchanged evaluator and end-to-end timings, accounting for input, transposition, resets, worker startup and reduction; treat marginal differences cautiously. The baseline’s four passing cases are not a proof: audit negative values, rectangular and one-dimensional matrices, repeated prefixes, k=0, extreme sums and 64-bit answer accumulation. Dispatch only on general input properties or estimated work, never case identity or expected outputs. Keep tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target and permissions unchanged.\",\"analysis\":\"The supplied source implements Problem A, counting contiguous submatrices with sum k; the other contest problems are outside scope. The baseline passes four correctness cases and averages 0.2493608 seconds across three tightly grouped measurements. No timed input dimensions, value distributions or profiles are supplied. Its O(MN²) enumeration, strided prefix accesses, repeated unordered_map lookups and per-band node allocation are plausible bottlenecks, not measured attributions. The complementary research directions are shape-aware contiguous enumeration, compact exact frequency counting, and balanced parallelism on the four-core ARM64 CPU. Negative entries prohibit an unconditional sliding-window replacement. Every valid input must remain exact; the maximum answer is 249500250000, requiring 64-bit accumulation. Combined performance must be measured independently.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"nonce\":\"cc4553cbc1f34d2b85974344fab6fca4\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"3646d52a3a8a514e7a2e2d5dfe46358c6910d19a0dff9e338a73aeebffd4badb\",\"session_id\":\"c0e9dfffccc040969abe9f6f54635671\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"bbccd6769d20998885cb639c6facc60b46a5896d7a397a83ee69d67e162ff5e4\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":9986,\"output_tokens\":6155,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":5346}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":16141,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
